WEBVTT

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.976
So, I get to New York City the next day,

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.239
I'm walking out of the Apple store,

00:19:04.263 --> 00:19:06.511
and this kid walks up to me
he's like, "Yo, D!"

00:19:06.535 --> 00:19:07.976
I'm like "Yeah?"

00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:10.976
He said, "If you really
held your breath that long,

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.976
why'd you come out of the water dry?"

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.976
I was like "What?"

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.976
(Laughter)

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.976
And that's my life. So --

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:23.132
(Laughter)

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:26.096
As a magician,
I try to show things to people

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.976
that seem impossible.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.481
And I think magic,

00:19:29.505 --> 00:19:32.976
whether I'm holding my breath
or shuffling a deck of cards,